46
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:53,360
and there are tons of
payouts that never stop.

47
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:56,600
I've been lining up from 3 a.m. every morning too,
you know.

48
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:57,460
Every morning?

49
00:02:57,780 --> 00:02:59,100
N-no, that's bad.

50
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,020
What I just said stays between us, got it?

51
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,960
If the Chief finds out I'm slacking off again,
he'll bite my head off.

52
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,140
But this is a live broadcast.

53
00:03:07,140 --> 00:03:08,160
Nowaaany!

54
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:11,520
Hey, cut that part! Cut it!

55
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:15,180
No, I mean, it's live,
so we can't edit it...

56
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:17,480
You're really going on
about how much you love it

57
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:18,940
Next, next!

58
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:19,640
Yes.

59
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:25,260
This is the Telephone Life Advice corner.

60
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:28,480
Ryo-san, we're counting on your advice too.

61
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:30,860
Leave it to me, ask me anything.

62
00:03:31,360 --> 00:03:32,720
That's reassuring to hear.

63
00:03:33,300 --> 00:03:36,260
Then let's call the
first caller Mr. A for now.

64
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,100
Mr. A.

65
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:37,940
Yes.

66
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:40,600
What is your concern?

67
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,520
Concern.

68
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:44,180
Well

69
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,240
Please, don't be shy.

70
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:48,220
Well, actually...

71
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:50,340
Are you nervous?

72
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:52,040
Relax, relax.

73
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:52,800
Yes.

74
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,380
Well...

75
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,760
What's the matter? Caller, please go ahead.

76
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,500
I know, but...

77
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:01,600
Well, you see, I...

78
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:03,100
How should I put this?

79
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:06,400
What kind of

80
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:09,260
You idiot, you came here for advice and

81
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:12,580
you just keep saying "um" and
"well." We're getting nowhere, you know!

82
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:16,320
A man should just spit it out,
I'm telling you, just spit it out!

83
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:17,220
Y-yes.

84
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:20,340
Fine, then I'll listen.
So hurry up and say it.

85
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:24,240
Actually well, there's someone I like...

86
00:04:24,860 --> 00:04:25,260
And?

87
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:29,640
The person I like... so I was
wondering what I should do about it.

88
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,880
