115
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:49,240
I lost my wallet,

116
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,280
and apparently my car got in an accident.

117
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,560
What am I supposed to do now?

118
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:52,820
Beats me, too.

119
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:53,680
So there you go.

120
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:54,720
Wait, hold on -

121
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:57,080
That's not an answer at all!

122
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:58,080
But, you know,

123
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,820
It's not like I care what you do

124
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,700
- it's none of my business.

125
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:02,540
But that's -

126
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:04,040
That's irresponsible!

127
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:04,760
What did you say?

128
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,500
Why should I care about
someone I've never even met?

129
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:10,240
Don't say such selfish things!

130
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:14,120
If you can't even sort out your own life,
what good are you?!

131
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:17,060
That's why you get laid off
and your wife runs off on you!

132
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,100
Got it?!

133
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:21,660
Well, thank you for that concise advice.

134
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,600
Shall we move on to the next one?

135
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,180
Yes, do that.

136
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,900
Well then,

137
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:32,860
It's time for the radio shopping corner!

138
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,920
Yes, hello, hello!

139
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:36,480
Listen and be convinced,
convinced all on your own!

140
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:40,520
