out people's names without permission!

250
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:27,240
Geez.

251
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:30,220
Eko-san?

252
00:11:31,740 --> 00:11:33,060
Wow, amazing, amazing.

253
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,180
Ugh, Ryo-chan, you idiot!

254
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:55,600
Excuse me, sir, would it be all
right if I listen to the radio?

255
00:11:57,500 --> 00:12:01,760
Well, it's a show that just started today,
but it's really entertaining.

256
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:04,180
Whatever you do, don't you dare fall asleep!

257
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:07,080
Kankichi Ryotsu again
tonight for two or three hours!

258
00:12:07,820 --> 00:12:10,160
No way! Why is Ryotsu here?!

259
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,940
Do you two know each other?

260
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:13,700
Yeah, well.

261
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:18,100
Well then, next fax.

262
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:21,080
From Ohanachaya,
pen name Yamadome Tatsuhiko.

263
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:25,820
The police seem to have strict hierarchies too,
but do you have any bad bosses?

264
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:30,180
Even though you can't even
handle a PC or a cell phone,

265
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,080
always just yelling all the time,

266
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,540
ten years of service

267
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,400
and still haven't achieved any real success,

268
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:37,400
just promoted through seniority alone,

269
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,860
what a pathetic boss, really.

270
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:41,760
That's you, Chief Ohara.

271
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:44,260
Yeah, you find those everywhere, don't you?

272
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,680
Useless bosses like that.

273
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,960
By the way, Chief Ohara is...

274
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,940
When he gets angry,
he makes a face like Omachi,

275
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:52,260
and he's got that little goatee
and acts so high and mighty.

276
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,380
If you ever actually see him,

277
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:55,060
point and laugh at him.

278
00:12:56,420 --> 00:13:01,160
Ryotsu, you bastard! How dare you say
whatever you want on the public airwaves!

279
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:05,160
I will never forgive this.

280
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:07,800
Driver, change of destination!

281
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:10,220
Head to this radio station immediately.

282
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:11,420
Y-yes!

283
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:16,260
Every last one of them is useless.

284
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:18,640
It's like a comic book, honestly.

285
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,960
Well then, commercial break.

286
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,680
What's the next segment again?

287
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:30,120
Hey, Ryo-chan!

288
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:31,860
Ryo-chan!

289
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:33,820
You guys!

290
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:36,660
You...!

291
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,240
That's harsh, senpai!

292
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,940
What do you think you're doing?!

293
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:41,080
What's the meaning of this?

294
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:45,200
Could everyone have been
listening to the radio?

295
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,060
Why is everyone here too?

296
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:49,920
I see. So that's how he got
all of them here in no time.

297
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,880
What? Let's throw those
people out right away.

298
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:58,220
As expected of Ryo-san!
He prepared a setup like this!

299
00:13:59,040 --> 00:13:59,600
Setup?

300
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:06,160
Ryo-san deliberately made his coworkers the butt of
the joke so they'd get angry and storm into the studio!

301
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:09,940
Wow, he came up with such a trick!
This is going to be an amazing show!

302
00:14:11,580 --> 00:14:15,160
Just who gave you permission
to be on the radio?!

303
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:18,820
Do you really think you can do this without permission from me,
your superior?

304
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,119
B-but Chief,

305
00:14:20,169 --> 00:14:23,260
Listeners want a personality like me!

306
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:26,600
The show is cancelled immediately.

307
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:26,980
No way.

308
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:30,480
Using someone as material
without permission,

309
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:32,620
we can't let this show go on.

310
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:33,720
That's right, senpai.

311
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:35,080
Please reflect on what you've done.

312
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,740
Come on, we're going back, Ryotsu.

313
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:38,560
Not allowed.

314
00:14:38,560 --> 00:14:41,440
Abandoning a live show halfway through,

315
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,700
I can't be that irresponsible.

316
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,500
You only talk back when it suits you.

317
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:49,260
If it comes to this,
I'll drag you back by force.

318
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:49,920
Come on.

319
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:51,820
I refuse.

320
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:53,420
No.

321
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:21,160
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuh...

322
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,900
Don't you remember me?

323
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:26,480
The phone-in life advice segment
from yesterday's broadcast.

324
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:29,680
You're the one I first talked to.

325
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,960
You said to call me
"Mr. A" for the sake of privacy.

326
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:38,420
I asked what to do about someone I like.

327
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,840
I think I remember something like that.

328
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:45,860
Just like you said, I finally worked
up the nerve and confessed today.

329
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:46,860
And then...

330
00:15:46,860 --> 00:15:47,880
And then...

331
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:49,580
So then,

332
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:51,540
looks like they got turned down

333
00:15:51,540 --> 00:15:53,620
You took your senior's irresponsible advice

334
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,820
a little too seriously, didn't you?

335
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,420
Poor thing.

336
00:15:56,420 --> 00:15:58,680
What are you thinking?

337
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:01,180
You've caused trouble not just for us,
but for ordinary citizens too.

338
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:02,400
Causing this kind of trouble!

339
00:16:03,520 --> 00:16:04,720
Don't pin this rejection

340
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,720
on me. It's unbearable!

341
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:09,060
Isn't it his fault that he got rejected?

342
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:09,900
This guy...

343
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:10,860
Be quiet!

344
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:14,420
How dare you toy with
my pure heart like that!

345
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:16,440
If it comes to this, I'll make you all

346
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:24,880
pay for this! Wait, calm down, let's talk this out calmly.
No, there's nothing left to talk about. I'm done, I'm just...

347
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:27,680
It's no use.
I've lost all my dreams and hope.

348
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:36,200
Because of your heartless remark, you see. That's why
you shouldn't have pushed ahead so far on what I said.

349
00:16:39,560 --> 00:16:42,600
It's insane,
the phones and faxes are about to overload!

350
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:46,220
They say we're getting a mountain of
questions asking whether the bomber is real.

351
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:48,640
Of course it's fake, isn't it?

352
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:50,920
It's a staged production, a production.

353
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:56,860
Wow, Ryo-san,
going as far as staging something like this!

354
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,240
Yes, hello?

355
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,260
Chief

356
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:04,780
What is this radio show that's on right now?

357
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,040
Not just Ryotsu, but the Bomb Mama too.

358
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,600
We're getting a flood of
inquiries at the station!

359
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,860
Was that real or not?

360
00:17:11,860 --> 00:17:15,160
Come on, Chief,
it's obviously fake, isn't it?

361
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:17,000
It was Ryo-san's staging.

362
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:17,860
Staging?

363
00:17:17,860 --> 00:17:20,560
Yes, something to make
everyone gasp in surprise.

364
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:22,500
He said he'd make it an amazing show.

365
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:24,580
Please don't worry.

366
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,520
We're going to a commercial.

367
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,600
Ryo-san, wrap it up for now.

368
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:32,160
Whoa, well then, here's a commercial break.

369
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:35,180
Ryo-tsukamichi's tonight, too, is 23 hours.

370
00:17:37,260 --> 00:17:38,440
Did you hear that?

371
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:42,720
If it were a real bomb scare, there's
no way they'd be running commercials.

372
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:44,800
That's true, but...

373
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:48,120
Still, everyone's jealous

374
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,900
I wanted to be on the radio too.

375
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:51,340
Hey, you lot, don't fall asleep!

376
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,600
Ryo-san's show tonight is
also two or three hours.

377
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:57,560
We interrupt this program
to bring you a news bulletin.

378
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,520
At around 6:30 this evening,

379
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:02,500
dynamite was stolen from a
construction site in Katsushika Ward.

380
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:08,400
According to witnesses, the culprit is a man in his twenties,
and the police are currently searching for him.

381
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:09,680
I repeat.

382
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:11,520
At around 6:30 this evening,

383
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,460
dynamite was stolen from a
construction site in Katsushika Ward.

384
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,120
Is this another of Ryo-san's stunts too?

385
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:16,140
No.

386
00:18:17,220 --> 00:18:18,640
Then who's that over there?

387
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,580
The real bomb culprit.

388
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:24,740
Yes, Katsushika Police Station.

389
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:27,620
There's a bomber at the radio station.

390
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:30,260
It was all staged, you know.

391
00:18:30,260 --> 00:18:33,280
There's no way a crazy story
like this could be true, right?

392
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,600
But right now,

393
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,780
please rest assured.

394
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:37,980
Ryotsu does this kind of
thing all the time anyway.

395
00:18:37,980 --> 00:18:39,920
It's obviously a lie.

396
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:44,160
No, it's no good.

397
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,960
They won't believe us at all.

398
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:48,180
What on earth should we do?

399
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:49,520
Wait a second.

400
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,580
Police officers' bargaining tactics

401
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:56,140
You can't just plan an incredible
accident like this on purpose!

402
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,020
So what do we do?

403
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,260
We keep the broadcast going as is.

404
00:19:00,260 --> 00:19:02,840
This is going to be an amazing broadcast.

405
00:19:03,400 --> 00:19:06,080
Just listen to what I have to say, will you?

406
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:06,960
Shut up!

407
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,960
Who'd want to hear your talk?

408
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,480
But listen, you

409
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:13,460
You shouldn't go off the deep end
just because you got turned down once.

410
00:19:13,460 --> 00:19:14,260
That's right.

411
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:17,140
I've been turned down
over and over again, too.

412
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:20,360
If you keep living,
you'll find a wonderful person someday.

413
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,240
Someday?

414
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:25,480
When, exactly? Today, or later on? When?

415
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:27,020
Well, that's...

416
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:31,160
Yeah, perfect. Reiko, you go out with him.

417
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:33,880
What are you doing, Ryo-chan?

418
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:39,900
It's fate, Reiko. If you become his lover,
this whole incident is solved.

419
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:41,740
Don't just say whatever you like!

420
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,620
Come on, just decide right here and now.

421
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:46,520
Decide what? Don't joke at a time like this!

422
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:46,840
Hey!

423
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:47,800
Whoa!

424
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:50,320
Every one of you is spouting nonsense!

425
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,580
You have no right to understand how I feel!

426
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:58,880
Hey, wait! If we just talk it out,
we can understand each other!

427
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:03,240
He's at it again!
This whole mess is your fault, you know!

428
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:06,140
Grr, you've got some nerve,
letting you talk like that!

429
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:08,720
Don't blame everyone else for everything!

430
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,010
If you hadn't come to me with that
stupid advice request in the first place,

431
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:14,100
none of this would have happened!

432
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:16,360
S-stupid, you say?

433
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:20,480
That's awful, Ryo-chan! The people
listening are seriously asking for advice!

434
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:23,520
That's right!
You're far too unserious, senpai!

435
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:28,580
Exactly! On the radio, every single
word you say has to be taken responsibly!

436
00:20:28,920 --> 00:20:30,320
And yet, senpai...!

437
00:20:31,360 --> 00:20:33,860
You lot are going to
side with this guy too?!

438
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:34,880
I won't forgive you!

439
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:38,300
Someone like you just
can't be let off the hook!

440
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,860
It's all your fault!

441
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:42,860
That's right, Ryotsu! Everyone's right!

442
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:44,600
It's all your responsibility!

443
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,900
C-Chief!

444
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,800
Going on the radio without
thinking things through,

445
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:52,920
making irresponsible remarks over and over and causing trouble for everyone.
This is the result!

446
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:57,420
And instead of reflecting, you brazenly
claim everyone else is to blame?

447
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:00,000
Enough with the nonsense! You idiot!

448
00:21:00,220 --> 00:21:01,720
I'm sorry, Chief!

449
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:02,940
Excuse me...

450
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:03,880
Yeah.

451
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:06,120
And you're no better, either.

452
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:09,560
Why would you hand over such an
important decision to someone else?

453
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:13,320
A man who can't even make
a simple decision himself

454
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,520
do you really think women will fall for him?

455
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:19,280
Okay! Now! Play the song!

456
00:21:19,380 --> 00:21:19,660
Yes!

457
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:29,060
Don't blame others for your own failures.

458
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:32,980
Even if others caused it,
you're the one who made the final decision.

459
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,720
At your age, you can't keep
relying on others like a child.

460
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:38,900
Life isn't all good times.

461
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:41,340
There's plenty of pain and suffering too.

462
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:45,100
But what good does it do to resent
people and act recklessly every time?

463
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:48,380
Even when it's hard,
you endure it and handle it yourself.

464
00:21:48,380 --> 00:21:50,160
That's what being an adult means.

465
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:57,460
I'm sorry.

466
00:21:58,040 --> 00:22:00,380
It was my fault, I'm sorry.

467
00:22:00,380 --> 00:22:01,320
We...

468
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:02,980
We're on this planet together.

469
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,580
As long as you understand.

470
00:22:05,580 --> 00:22:07,580
Come on, life is long.

471
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:09,300
You can still start over.

472
00:22:19,880 --> 00:22:21,420
Just as expected of the Chief.

473
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,880
Problem solved beautifully

474
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:31,340
Thank goodness, really. For a moment there,
I didn't know how it would turn out, but the Chief took it all on himself.

475
00:22:31,340 --> 00:22:33,420
That's a wrap Okay.

476
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:43,440
What a heartwarming story, typical of a mass-produced show.
Well, shall we go? No, never mind, the documentary...

477
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:48,140
...brought to you with a documentary touch.
But the Chief's lines were a bit cheesy, weren't they?

478
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:51,760
...weren't they?
The BGM was a bit cheesy too, Fujiyama.

479
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:57,060
Mocchi! Hey, what are you doing? What do you mean,
what? I'm continuing the show.

480
00:22:57,060 --> 00:23:05,700
Kaz, are you still coming? You idiot!
Come on! I don't want to. Just come!

481
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:14,740
I told you, I'm not going, the broadcast is canceled!
I said I won't allow you to keep going! We're on air, we're on air!

482
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,080
Eeeh?

483
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:19,240
M-me, on the radio?

484
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,280
Yes!

485
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:23,340
that presence that even
Ryo-san can't talk back to,

486
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:25,780
and that warmth that even the
bomber was moved to tears by.

487
00:23:25,780 --> 00:23:28,800
Please, do appear on our new show!

488
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:31,900
The show's title is
"Chief Ohara, I'll Beat You!"

489
00:23:31,900 --> 00:23:33,000
That settles it.

490
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,820
No, I'm not the kind of...

491
00:23:35,620 --> 00:23:36,660
Please, we're begging you.

492
00:23:36,660 --> 00:23:40,500
The times call for DJs like Ohara-san.

493
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:41,440
Please.

494
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:43,360
But...

495
00:23:44,740 --> 00:23:47,720
So in the end my show gets
cancelled after just one episode?

496
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:48,880
It can't be helped.

497
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,500
After causing that kind of trouble.

498
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:51,480
You brought it on yourself.

499
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:55,520
But the Chief's persuasion was really something,
wasn't it?

500
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:57,160
Please do join us.

501
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:59,600
Well, it's over

502
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:01,980
Ahahahaha!

503
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:22,580
Why does Lemon-chan,
a kindergartner, love period dramas?

504
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:28,700
Why is the Chief's little
mustache slightly small?

505
00:24:31,280 --> 00:24:36,560
Why does Honda's personality
change when he rides a motorcycle?

506
00:24:37,940 --> 00:24:43,400
Why does Hikurashi Neruo only
wake up once every four years?

507
00:24:44,740 --> 00:24:45,640
I wonder why.

508
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:52,580
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

509
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:56,360
but he lends out tanks
and fighter planes easily.

510
00:24:56,360 --> 00:25:00,260
I wonder why.

511
00:25:02,180 --> 00:25:07,000
Reiko is incredibly rich,

512
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:10,740
but she works at the police box.

513
00:25:10,740 --> 00:25:12,540
I wonder why.

514
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:16,300
I wonder why, I wonder why.

515
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:19,640
Why, why, why, why do I wonder?

516
00:25:29,920 --> 00:25:30,720
Oh no!

517
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:34,700
We drank away all the money
we collected for the trip!

518
00:25:35,140 --> 00:25:39,240
We have to take everyone on that trip somehow,
or we're in big trouble!

519
00:25:39,760 --> 00:25:43,480
Who on earth came up with an
octopus trip to Atami, anyway?

520
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:47,260
See you on the next Atami octopus trip!

521
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:54,940
Thank you.

